{
  "id": "hydraulic_oil_pump___horsepower_vs__pressure_and_v",
  "title": "Hydraulic Oil Pump - Horsepower vs. Pressure and Volume Flow",
  "description": "Calculate the power required for hydraulic pumping based on flow rate, pressure, and efficiency.",
  "type": "calculator-table",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "# Hydraulic Oil Pump - Horsepower vs. Pressure and Volume Flow\n\nThe power required for hydraulic pumping.\n\n## Formula\n\n**PHP = q × p / ((μ / 100) × 1714)**\n\nWhere:\n- **PHP** = horsepower (HP)\n- **q** = flow (gpm)\n- **p** = required pressure (psi)\n- **μ** = overall efficiency (%)\n\n## Example\n\nFor a pump with flow 20 gpm and 1500 psi increase in pressure at 100% efficiency:\n\nPHP = (20 × 1500) / 1714 = 17.5 HP"
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "flow",
          "label": "Flow Rate",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "gpm",
          "defaultValue": 20
        },
        {
          "id": "pressure",
          "label": "Pressure",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "psi",
          "defaultValue": 1500
        },
        {
          "id": "efficiency",
          "label": "Efficiency",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "%",
          "defaultValue": 100
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "horsepower",
          "label": "Horsepower Required",
          "formula": "inputs.flow * inputs.pressure / ((inputs.efficiency / 100) * 1714)",
          "unit": "HP",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "datatable",
      "headers": [
        "Flow (gpm)",
        "Pressure (psi)",
        "Efficiency (%)",
        "Horsepower (HP)"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          10,
